TITLE:: PlayableNote
SUMMARY:: A timed MIDI note used for sequencer playback.
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/SequencePlayer, Classes/Sequencer

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PlayableNote:: holds the timing and MIDI data for a single note: when it starts, when it stops, which key to play, and how hard. Times are expressed in beats on the LINK::Classes/TempoClock:: (the same unit used by LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: and the piano roll).

A note is STRONG::playable:: only after TELETYPE::stopTime_:: has been set. Until then, TELETYPE::isPlayable:: is false and the slice and playhead query methods all return false. LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote:: creates a TELETYPE::PlayableNote:: internally and keeps its start and stop times in sync when the note is moved or resized on the roll.

Playback scheduling uses half-open intervals: the note is considered active while the playhead satisfies TELETYPE::startTime <= t < stopTime::. TELETYPE::startsInSlice:: uses TELETYPE::sliceStartTime <= startTime < sliceStopTime::; TELETYPE::stopsInSlice:: uses TELETYPE::sliceStartTime < stopTime <= sliceStopTime:: so a note-off at the slice start is excluded but one at the slice end is included.

NOTE::
You can run the unit tests for TELETYPE::PlayableNote:: by running:
CODE::
(
UnitTest.reportPasses_(false);
PlayableNoteUnitTests.run;
)
::
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::PlayableNote::. The note is not playable until TELETYPE::stopTime_:: is set.

ARGUMENT:: startTime
The beat at which the note starts (a LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::).

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
The MIDI note number (0–127).

ARGUMENT:: velocity
The MIDI velocity (0–127).

returns::
A new instance.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: isPlayable
Whether this note has a stop time and can take part in playback queries.

returns::
true if TELETYPE::stopTime:: is set, otherwise false.

METHOD:: noteNumber
The MIDI note number.

returns::
An LINK::Classes/Integer::.

METHOD:: startTime
The beat at which the note starts.

returns::
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::.

METHOD:: startTime_
Sets the beat at which the note starts.

ARGUMENT:: value
The start time in beats.

returns::
This instance (for chaining).

METHOD:: stopTime
The beat at which the note stops.

returns::
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::, or nil if not yet set.

METHOD:: stopTime_
Sets the beat at which the note stops, making the note playable.

ARGUMENT:: value
The stop time in beats.

returns::
This instance (for chaining).

METHOD:: velocity
The MIDI velocity. Setting replaces the stored velocity.

ARGUMENT:: value
When setting, an LINK::Classes/Integer:: MIDI velocity.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Integer::.

METHOD:: shouldBePlaying
Whether the note should sound at a given playhead position.

Returns false if the note is not playable. Otherwise returns true when TELETYPE::startTime <= playheadTime < stopTime::.

ARGUMENT:: playheadTime
The current position of the playhead, in beats.

returns::
true or false.

METHOD:: startsInSlice
Whether the note's start time falls within a scheduling slice.

Returns false if the note is not playable. Otherwise returns true when TELETYPE::sliceStartTime <= startTime < sliceStopTime::. LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: uses this to decide when to send note-on events for a slice.

ARGUMENT:: sliceStartTime
The start of the slice, in beats (inclusive).

ARGUMENT:: sliceStopTime
The end of the slice, in beats (exclusive).

returns::
true or false.

METHOD:: stopsInSlice
Whether the note's stop time falls within a scheduling slice.

Returns false if the note is not playable. Otherwise returns true when TELETYPE::sliceStartTime < stopTime <= sliceStopTime::. A stop time equal to TELETYPE::sliceStartTime:: is excluded; a stop time equal to TELETYPE::sliceStopTime:: is included. LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer:: uses this to decide when to send note-off events for a slice.

ARGUMENT:: sliceStartTime
The start of the slice, in beats (exclusive for the stop time).

ARGUMENT:: sliceStopTime
The end of the slice, in beats (inclusive for the stop time).

returns::
true or false.


EXAMPLES::

CODE::
// Create a note from beat 4 to beat 8
var note = PlayableNote(4, 60, 100).stopTime_(8);

note.isPlayable;           // true
note.shouldBePlaying(5);   // true  — playhead inside [4, 8)
note.shouldBePlaying(8);   // false — stop time is exclusive

// Slice [4, 4.25) — one sixteenth note at default SequencePlayer delta
note.startsInSlice(4, 4.25);  // true  — note-on in this slice
note.stopsInSlice(4, 4.25);   // false — note-off is later

note.stopsInSlice(8, 8.25);      // false — stop at slice start is excluded
note.stopsInSlice(7.75, 8.25);   // true  — note-off in this slice
note.stopsInSlice(7.75, 8);      // true  — stop at slice end is included

// Build a sequence for SequencePlayer (see LINK::Classes/SequencePlayer::)
[
    PlayableNote(0, 60, 100).stopTime_(4),
    PlayableNote(4, 64, 90).stopTime_(8)
];
::
